schema: "0.4"
id: trd-authoring-01-desktop-toolbar
type: image
quality: high

# therobotdrafts authoring UX — desktop command surface mockup.
# Consumes: design-conventions §1.1 silhouettes + §2.1 Okabe-Ito kind palette,
# Lena's iconography system (ticket e94fe1b8) incl the §B reserved non-kind UI
# color channel, and Yuki's toolbar flow (ticket 1085589f). UML class/bubble core.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    PROFESSIONAL 3D developer tool — a VR/desktop "UML IDE" where a codebase is
    navigated as packed spheres (bubbles). This is NOT a game and NOT a cartoon.
    The aesthetic is calm, premium, and technical: a dark neutral workspace with
    volumetric depth, crisp signed-distance-field labels, restrained chrome.

    THE ONE INVIOLABLE RULE: semantic color belongs ONLY to the bubbles (element
    kind). All UI chrome — toolbar, panels, rails, dividers — is ACHROMATIC
    (neutral grey/graphite, faint translucency), so it never competes with or is
    mistaken for a kind hue. Selection/feedback uses a reserved channel: white
    rim → cyan, never a kind color.
  text: |
    A 16:9 mockup of the desktop authoring screen for a 3D "bubble" UML IDE.

    BACKGROUND CANVAS (fills the frame):
    - A dark graphite 3D space (#15181C → #1E2329 subtle vignette) with soft
      volumetric depth and a faint ground-plane grid receding into distance.
    - Floating packed spheres ("bubbles") representing code elements, colored
      STRICTLY by the Okabe-Ito kind palette, each with its distinct silhouette:
        • Package: large translucent FROSTED sphere, slate (#6E7B8B), child
          bubbles faintly visible inside it.
        • Class: opaque solid matte sphere, blue (#0072B2).
        • Interface: sphere with a hollow dashed equatorial band, sky (#56B4E9).
        • Enum: faceted low-poly gem-like sphere, orange (#E69F00).
        • Struct: sphere with a flat polar cap, teal (#009E73).
        • Function/method: small slightly-emissive sphere, green (#2CA02C).
        • Field: smallest flattened sphere, yellow-green (#BCBD22).
    - One class bubble is SELECTED: a bright white→cyan contrasting outline rim
      (the reserved selection channel — NOT a kind color). Its sibling bubbles
      are slightly dimmed/desaturated to show focus context.
    - A few thin relationship tubes connect bubbles (solid line, small arrowhead).
    - Short crisp SDF labels float on the nearest/largest bubbles only
      (e.g. "auth", "Session", "login") — most bubbles are unlabeled (label budget).

    LEFT VERTICAL TOOLBAR RAIL (the command surface — achromatic, ~56px wide):
    A slim translucent graphite rail pinned to the left edge, monochrome icon
    buttons on a 24px glyph / 32px hit grid, grouped with faint dividers:
      • Select (arrow cursor) — LIT/active with a soft white-cyan ring (home state).
      • [divider]  Create group: Add-node (a ＋ over a small bubble),
        Connect (two dots joined by a line).
      • [divider]  Edit group: Delete (trash), Undo (↶), Redo (↷)
        — Undo/Redo shown faintly DIMMED (empty history).
      • [divider]  Output group: Project-to-2D (a bubble morphing into a
        rectangle) — dimmed/disabled (nothing selected to project).
    Icons are clean 2px-stroke monochrome pictograms, pixel-crisp, NO color fill.

    TOP STRIP (thin, achromatic):
    - A breadcrumb HUD showing the qualified path: "auth ›  Session ›  login",
      small humanist sans-serif, muted grey-white text.

    CREATION-PALETTE FLYOUT (open, anchored just right of the Add-node button):
    A small dark translucent panel listing the UML-core kinds as rows, each row =
    its §2.1-colored kind glyph + label: ○ Package, ● Class (row highlighted as
    default), ◐ Interface, ⬢ Enum, ◑ Struct, · Function, · Field. One row
    ("Field") is dimmed/struck to show it is illegal in the current parent. The
    swatch on each row is the exact kind hue+silhouette so the palette previews
    what the bubble will look like.

    OVERALL:
    - Mood: focused, spacious, premium dev-tool (think a 3D Linear/Figma, not a
      game HUD). Generous negative space. No skeuomorphism, no neon clutter.
    - Only the bubbles carry saturated color; every control is graphite + white.
    - Typography: clean humanist sans-serif, excellent small-size legibility.
  provider_options:
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"
    style: "natural"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    palette_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Bubbles use the exact Okabe-Ito kind hues AND distinct silhouettes (frosted package, solid class, banded interface, faceted enum, polar-cap struct); each kind read at least twice (hue+shape)"}
    reserved_channel: {weight: 3, description: "All UI chrome is achromatic graphite/white; selection is a white→cyan rim, never a kind hue; no UI element colored like a kind"}
    layout_fidelity: {weight: 2, description: "Left vertical rail grouped Select / Create / Edit / Output; creation-palette flyout with kind rows incl one dimmed illegal kind; breadcrumb HUD on top"}
    premium_tool_feel: {weight: 2, description: "Calm dark premium developer-tool aesthetic with 3D depth; not a game HUD, not cartoonish"}
  reject_if:
    - "UI chrome (toolbar/panels) tinted with kind colors or rainbow chrome"
    - "cartoon/game aesthetic, neon clutter, or skeuomorphic textures"
    - "bubbles all the same shape (silhouette redundancy missing)"
    - "labels illegible or every bubble labeled (no label budget)"

tags: [trd, authoring-ux, desktop, toolbar, bubble-view, uml, mockup, ui]
